.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-IDCARD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-idcard
.Nd make or check an identity card for a signing key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis idcard
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Fl -name Ar name
.Op Fl -orcid Ar id
.Op Fl -email Ar address
.Op Fl -url Ar url
.Op Fl -affil Ar text
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl f
.Nm noqtis idcard
.Fl -verify Ar card
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis idcard
writes an identity card
.Pq Ql noqtis-idcard-1 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5 :
the public key of
.Ar key
with your name and, when given, your ORCID iD, e-mail address, web page
and affiliation, signed by
.Ar key
itself.
Publish the card beside your capsules (on your web page, in a
repository, with a paper) and give the SHA-256 of the key somewhere
people already know you by.
.Xr noqtis-check 1
.Fl -card
then says who sealed a capsule.
.Pp
A card is self-signed: its signature shows that whoever holds the key
wrote it and that nothing in it changed since, not that the name is
true.
What ties the name to the key is the key's SHA-256 that you published,
or a public key the checker already trusts
.Pq Fl p .
Its signature is made under its own context,
.Ql noqtis-idcard-1 ,
so a card is never taken for a seal or a key statement, nor they for a
card.
The signature is checked before the card is written, and the secret key
is never in it.
.Pp
The creation time is
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
when set, as for
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
else the clock.
.Pp
With
.Fl -verify ,
.Nm
checks
.Ar card
and prints the fields it holds, its key's algorithm and the SHA-256 of
its public key (as
.Xr noqtis-inspect 1
prints a seal's).
With
.Fl p ,
the card must also be for that key.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
The secret signing key the card is for: ML-DSA, SLH-DSA or a hybrid,
not Ed25519 alone.
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
Its public key (default
.Ar key Ns Pa .pub ) ;
with
.Fl -verify ,
the key the card must be for.
.It Fl -name Ar name
Your name as you want it shown: 1 to 255 bytes of UTF-8, no control
character, no space at either end.
.It Fl -orcid Ar id
Your ORCID iD, as
.Ql 0000-0002-1825-0097
or its
.Ql https://orcid.org/
address; its last character must be its ISO 7064 MOD 11-2 check digit
(X for 10).
The card holds the bare iD.
.It Fl -email Ar address
An e-mail address
.Ql local@domain.tld ,
at most 254 bytes, no space.
.It Fl -url Ar url
A web page: an
.Ql https://
address with a host, at most 1024 bytes, no space.
.It Fl -affil Ar text
Your affiliation, as
.Fl -name .
.It Fl o Ar file , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar file
Write the card to
.Ar file
(mode 0644) instead of standard output.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace
.Ar file
if it exists.
.It Fl -verify Ar card
Check a card instead of making one.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
The card was written, or it verifies.
.It 1
The card does not verify, is not a card, or is for another key than
.Fl p .
.It 2
A usage error, a field out of its limits, a key file that cannot be
read, keys that are not a pair or not post-quantum, or a file that
cannot be read or written.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis idcard -k me --name "Ada Lovelace" \e
    --orcid 0000-0002-1825-0097 --url https://example.org/ada -o me.card
$ noqtis idcard --verify me.card
name     Ada Lovelace
orcid    0000-0002-1825-0097
url      https://example.org/ada
created  2026-10-30T12:00:00Z
alg      ML-DSA-65
key      4587412415426cb336627c940b6a8c921c903d6149cc3e632a891d6de86fe710
me.card: OK (self-signed: compare the key with the one its holder gave)
$ noqtis check -p me.pub --card me.card results
.Ed
.Pp
An iD with a wrong check digit is refused:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis idcard -k me --name Ada --orcid 0000-0002-1825-0098
noqtis idcard: --orcid 0000-0002-1825-0098: give an ORCID iD such as
0000-0002-1825-0097 (or its https://orcid.org/ address) whose last
character is its check digit
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr nqcard 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
